<div class="py-8 sm:py-16 lg:py-24">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-site px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 items-center gap-8 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <!-- Left Column - Skeleton -->
      <div class="relative h-132 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl p-6 sm:h-143 xl:h-118">
        <div class="absolute inset-s-0 bottom-0">
          <img
            src="https://cdn.flyonui.com/fy-assets/blocks/marketing-ui/faq/gradient-bg.png"
            class="h-75 w-full"
            alt="gradient bg circle"
          />
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-1">
          <p class="text-sm font-medium">FAQS</p>
          <h2 class="text-5xl font-semibold">
            Frequently Asked Questions❔
          </h2>
        </div>
        <div class="absolute inset-e-0 bottom-0">
          <img
            src="https://cdn.flyonui.com/fy-assets/blocks/marketing-ui/faq/faq-5.png"
            alt="Alena Lubin"
            class="h-77 w-auto"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
      <!-- Right Column - FAQ Content -->
      <div
        class="w-full divide-y rounded-xl shadow-sm"
        x-data="{ open: 'what-is-larasaas' }"
      >
        <div>
          <button
            type="button"
            class="inline-flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-x-4 px-5 py-4 text-start font-medium"
            id="what-is-larasaas"
            x-on:click="open = open === 'what-is-larasaas' ? null : 'what-is-larasaas'"
            x-bind:aria-expanded="(open === 'what-is-larasaas').toString()"
            aria-controls="what-is-larasaas-content"
          >
            What is LaraSaas? Why do I need a LaraSaas Boilerplate?
            <span
              class="icon-[tabler--chevron-right] size-4.5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-300 rtl:rotate-180"
              x-bind:class="open === 'what-is-larasaas' ? 'rotate-90' : ''"
            ></span>
          </button>
          <div
            id="what-is-larasaas-content"
            class="w-full overflow-hidden"
            role="region"
            aria-labelledby="what-is-larasaas"
            x-show="open === 'what-is-larasaas'"
            x-collapse
          >
            <div class="px-8 pb-4">
              <p class="text-base">
                LaraSaas is a Laravel boilerplate specifically designed to help
                you launch your SaaS application quickly and efficiently.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <button
            type="button"
            class="inline-flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-x-4 px-5 py-4 text-start font-medium"
            id="is-demo-available"
            x-on:click="open = open === 'is-demo-available' ? null : 'is-demo-available'"
            x-bind:aria-expanded="(open === 'is-demo-available').toString()"
            aria-controls="is-demo-available-content"
          >
            Is there a demo available?
            <span
              class="icon-[tabler--chevron-right] size-4.5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-300 rtl:rotate-180"
              x-bind:class="open === 'is-demo-available' ? 'rotate-90' : ''"
            ></span>
          </button>
          <div
            id="is-demo-available-content"
            class="w-full overflow-hidden"
            role="region"
            aria-labelledby="is-demo-available"
            x-cloak
            x-show="open === 'is-demo-available'"
            x-collapse
          >
            <div class="px-8 pb-4">
              <p class="text-base">
                Yes, we offer a comprehensive demo that showcases all the
                features and capabilities of our platform. You can access it
                through our website and explore the interface firsthand.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <button
            type="button"
            class="inline-flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-x-4 px-5 py-4 text-start font-medium"
            id="payment-providers"
            x-on:click="open = open === 'payment-providers' ? null : 'payment-providers'"
            x-bind:aria-expanded="(open === 'payment-providers').toString()"
            aria-controls="payment-providers-content"
          >
            Which payment providers are supported?
            <span
              class="icon-[tabler--chevron-right] size-4.5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-300 rtl:rotate-180"
              x-bind:class="open === 'payment-providers' ? 'rotate-90' : ''"
            ></span>
          </button>
          <div
            id="payment-providers-content"
            class="w-full overflow-hidden"
            role="region"
            aria-labelledby="payment-providers"
            x-cloak
            x-show="open === 'payment-providers'"
            x-collapse
          >
            <div class="px-8 pb-4">
              <p class="text-base">
                We support major payment providers including Stripe, PayPal, and
                Square. Our platform is designed to be flexible and can be
                integrated with additional payment gateways based on your needs.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <button
            type="button"
            class="inline-flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-x-4 px-5 py-4 text-start font-medium"
            id="codebase-distribution"
            x-on:click="open = open === 'codebase-distribution' ? null : 'codebase-distribution'"
            x-bind:aria-expanded="(open === 'codebase-distribution').toString()"
            aria-controls="codebase-distribution-content"
          >
            How is the codebase distributed?
            <span
              class="icon-[tabler--chevron-right] size-4.5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-300 rtl:rotate-180"
              x-bind:class="open === 'codebase-distribution' ? 'rotate-90' : ''"
            ></span>
          </button>
          <div
            id="codebase-distribution-content"
            class="w-full overflow-hidden"
            role="region"
            aria-labelledby="codebase-distribution"
            x-cloak
            x-show="open === 'codebase-distribution'"
            x-collapse
          >
            <div class="px-8 pb-4">
              <p class="text-base">
                The codebase is distributed through a private repository system.
                Upon purchase, you'll receive access to the full source code and
                all future updates through our version control system.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <button
            type="button"
            class="inline-flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center justify-between gap-x-4 px-5 py-4 text-start font-medium"
            id="integration-question"
            x-on:click="open = open === 'integration-question' ? null : 'integration-question'"
            x-bind:aria-expanded="(open === 'integration-question').toString()"
            aria-controls="integration-question-content"
          >
            I want to integrate LaraSaas into my existing project. Should I buy
            it?
            <span
              class="icon-[tabler--chevron-right] size-4.5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-300 rtl:rotate-180"
              x-bind:class="open === 'integration-question' ? 'rotate-90' : ''"
            ></span>
          </button>
          <div
            id="integration-question-content"
            class="w-full overflow-hidden"
            role="region"
            aria-labelledby="integration-question"
            x-cloak
            x-show="open === 'integration-question'"
            x-collapse
          >
            <div class="px-8 pb-4">
              <p class="text-base">
                While it's possible to integrate LaraSaas into existing
                projects, it's primarily designed as a standalone boilerplate.
                We recommend starting fresh with LaraSaas for the best
                experience and to fully utilize all features.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
